   "resumo_en": "The Godfathers, also known as the Orange Album, is the fifth studio album by English rock band the Godfathers, released on German label Intercord in 1993. It was the band's first out of two albums for the label, and the only studio album to feature drummer Ali Byworth. It has become known as the Orange Album because of the citrus fruit appearing on its cover. The album was reissued in 2013 through the Godfathers' own Godfathers Recordings label, including a bonus disc of demos and live tracks.",
